  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Third Rock From The Sun** (1 other source): Uploader lists this track as the Hendrix tune 'Third Stone from the Sun', played with the Shady Horns and Maceo Parker [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Hatrick**: back after 87 archived shows (1232 days); rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Third Rock From The Sun**: back after 22 archived shows (394 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Uptown Up**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Shake Everything You've Got**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Night Time Is The Right Time**: back after 38 archived shows (535 days); rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **There Was A Time**: back after 73 archived shows (973 days); rare: 8 archived performances [3]\n- **Pass The Peas**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **do you want to hear one more?**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2013-08-17.DPA4021s-SD722.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 14 songs; 90 min [1]\n- **soulive2013-08-17.DPA4021s-SD722.flac24**: source not stated; 13 songs; 90 min [2]. Said about its sound: Uploader warns this and his three other Equifunk 2013 recordings are far from his best, with shortcomings [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The Shady Horns joined Soulive, with special guest Maceo Parker sitting in [1]\n- The Shady Horns joined Soulive, with special guest Maceo Parker sitting in [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2013-08-17.DPA4021s-SD722.flac16**: taped by ericv; transferred by ericv; source: B&K(DPA) 4021s (clamped to low mic stand center front lip of stage, ~1' height and 110 degrees) > Sound Devices 722 (v2.67, 24bit/96kHz) > CF card / WAV files [1]\n- **soulive2013-08-17.DPA4021s-SD722.flac24**: taped by ericv; transferred by ericv; source: B&K(DPA) 4021s (clamped to low mic stand center front lip of stage, ~1' height and 110 degrees) > Sound Devices 722 (v2.67, 24bit/96kHz) > CF card / WAV files [2]",
